826:are known to the attacker. For key recovery, the attacker should find a vector $(G, F, -\rho(\gamma)) $ which satisfies the equation  $F\circ\tilde{H}= G+\gamma\pmod q$.
827:%Expanding the quaternion equation $F\circ\tilde{H}= G+\gamma\,\,(mod\,\,q)$ for a given quaternion $\tilde{H}$ is the only way for attacking  and finding a suitable key for decryption.\\
