In the sequel,  we explain how the key recovery of our cryptosystem is formulated as a shortest vector problem in a certain special form of a lattice.

 The parameters $n$, $p$, $q$, $d_f$, $d_g$, $d_\phi$  and the public key
$\tilde{H}=F^{-1} \circ G + \vartheta$, where $F\circ F^{-1}=F^{-1}\circ F= 1\pmod J$,
%=\left[ \begin{array}{cccc}
