Due to the hybrid structure of the BQTRU lattice, recovering the private  key in our cryptosystem leads to solving SVP in the expanded lattice which is at least  $(2+\log_2 n)$ times larger than  the dimension of the NTRU lattice with equivalent parameters. This increasing in the dimension of the lattice force a high cost  to the attacker using a lattice attack in this cryptosystem. As a result of this expansion, this cryptosystem achieves high security against lattice attacks. Also we can reduce the size of the private keys without violating the system security and use larger message. Hence, message protection is feasible through larger polynomials increasing message security.
